1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,583
First, a confession.

2
00:00:01,603 --> 00:00:02,006
Right now,

3
00:00:02,006 --> 00:00:02,791
you are moving.

4
00:00:02,811 --> 00:00:03,475
Fast.

5
00:00:03,495 --> 00:00:04,675
Earth spins once a day,

6
00:00:04,695 --> 00:00:05,905
and at the equator,

7
00:00:05,925 --> 00:00:07,149
the ground beneath you travels

8
00:00:07,149 --> 00:00:09,325
about 1,670 kilometers per

9
00:00:09,325 --> 00:00:09,551
hour.

10
00:00:10,251 --> 00:00:11,093
The farther you are from

11
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:11,831
the equator,

12
00:00:11,851 --> 00:00:13,080
the slower you go.

13
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,210
New York cruises at about

14
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:15,540
1,270.

15
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,357
London, about 1,040.

16
00:00:17,377 --> 00:00:18,397
At the North Pole,

17
00:00:18,417 --> 00:00:19,316
you're just turning in a

18
00:00:19,316 --> 00:00:20,051
very slow circle.

19
00:00:20,751 --> 00:00:22,098
And that's just the spin.

20
00:00:22,118 --> 00:00:23,347
Earth also races around the

21
00:00:23,347 --> 00:00:25,213
Sun at about 107,000

22
00:00:25,213 --> 00:00:26,268
kilometers per hour,

23
00:00:26,288 --> 00:00:27,240
while the Sun drags us

24
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,888
around the galaxy even faster.

25
00:00:28,908 --> 00:00:30,680
Relax: nobody is stopping

26
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:31,189
those.

27
00:00:31,209 --> 00:00:31,608
Today.

28
00:00:32,308 --> 00:00:33,169
So why don't you feel

29
00:00:33,169 --> 00:00:33,566
it?

30
00:00:33,586 --> 00:00:34,863
Because everything moves with

31
00:00:34,863 --> 00:00:36,216
you: the ground,

32
00:00:36,216 --> 00:00:36,558
the air,

33
00:00:36,558 --> 00:00:37,348
the oceans.

34
00:00:37,368 --> 00:00:38,710
It's like a smooth flight.

35
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:39,531
You can sip coffee at

36
00:00:39,531 --> 00:00:41,711
900 km/h without spilling a

37
00:00:41,711 --> 00:00:42,023
drop.

38
00:00:42,723 --> 00:00:44,175
You already know this feeling.
